'''Yarrum Tower''' was a [[pirate]] base<ref name="The Jellyfruit Pursuit" /> and market<ref name="Galactic Training">''[[Star Wars: Young Jedi Adventures: Galactic Training]]''</ref> on the [[planet]] [[Yarrum]].<ref name="The Jellyfruit Pursuit" />

{{Loc-stub}}
==History==
===Stolen Seeds===
When [[Cyrus Vuundir|Taborr Val-Dorn]] had stolen the [[Sparkle-fire seed]]s, he went in his ship, the ''[[Iron Talon]]'', to Yarrum Tower, intending to sell them. Val-Dorn met with a [[Unidentified Chagrian pirate|Chagrian pirate]], and asked him about selling the seeds, however the pirate merely mocked him for attempting to sell the item, which he saw as worthless. Later, when [[Kai Brightstar]], [[Lys Solay]] and [[Nubs]] arrived in pursuit of the stolen seeds, they boarded his ship, which was resting on a docking ring. Following a brief fight, the three attempted an escape, however Nubs had fallen off the edge of the ''[[Firehawk]]'' and Val-Dorn had taken Brightstar's [[Kai's first lightsaber|lightsaber]]. Brightstar, forced to choose, ultimately chose to save his friend before they left together back to [[Tenoo]].<ref name="Yoda's Mission">{{YJA|Yoda's Mission}}</ref>

===Disguised Jedi===
[[Kai Brightstar]], [[Lys Solay]], [[Nubs]], and [[Nash Durango]] disguised themselves as pirates outside Yarrum Tower, and took a turbo lift up to the marketplace. The Jedi and Durango walked in, and, when noticed by a [[Unidentified Twi'lek guard|Twi'lek guard]], who asked where they were going. Durango told the group to act threatening, and the Jedi  started to growl while Durango threatened the guard. The guard grumbled and accepted them in, noting how she was not paid enough to deal with this. As group entered, Brightstar tapped on a [[teapot]] at a [[Unidentified Chagrian pirate|Chagrian pirate]]'s stall, much to the Chagrian's displeasure. The Chagrian grumbled at Brightstar, and Durango reminded Brightstar that they were meant to act tough in disguise, which caused Brightstar to smash the teapot in his attempt, only angering the Chagrian further. Durango dragged Brightstar away, before she bumped into a [[Abednedo]] [[Chigg|pirate]], who despite being perceived as threatening by Durango, quickly welcomed the younger pirates and offered them the location of [[Cyrus Vuundir|Taborr Val-Dorn]], [[EB-3]], and [[Pord]] who had sold him a [[Jellyfruit]] upon request. Durango expressed annoyance at Val-Dorn stealing the Jellyfruit rather than sharing them, before they walked upon to his stall. Val-Dorn offered Brightstar a sample, and tossed him a fruit, which Brightstar attempted to catch, however his disguise fell off in the process. Brightstar was recognized by Val-Dorn, who announced him as a Jedi, upsetting the nearby patrons. Once the Jedi and Durango had their cover blown, they chased after a fleeing Val-Dorn and Pord, who rode on a cart full of Jellyfruit pushed by EB-3, accidentally smashed a plate at the Chagrian's stall as they whizzed by, further upsetting the Chagrian. As Durango ran past, she apologized to the Chagrian, who simply sighed. Val-Dorn and Port mocked the Jedi and Durango, when EB-3 lost control of the cart, sending it spiraling towards the edge. However, as it went over the edge, the Jedi had grabbed it and carried it back up onto the platform. Solay and Durango revealed that Val-Dorn stole the fruit from an [[Weebo|elderly farmer]] and her [[Weebo's grandson|grandchild]], which caused the other pirates to laugh at Val-Dorn. Val-Dorn attempted to state that his feat was impressive, but was ignored by the other pirates. As the Jedi and Durango were leaving, Durango offered Val-Dorn a Jellyfruit, restating how Jellyfruit were meant to be shared, before leaving with the Jedi to return to the [[Jellyfruit Festival]]. Pord asked Val-Dorn to share the Jellyfruit with him, but Val-Dorn declined, much to his dismay.<ref name="The Jellyfruit Pursuit" />

